{"name":"Bianca","hex":"#f4efe0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bianca","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Italian.","A surname from Italian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bianca"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bianca","blocks":[{"text":"Bianca is a feminine given name. It means \"white\" and is an Italian cognate of Blanche. It is known in the Anglosphere as a character in William Shakespeare's The Taming of the Shrew. It came to greater notice in the 1970s, due to public figures such as Bianca Jagger."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d2/Frederick_leighton-bianca_c1881_0876.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bianca"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"Bianca":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Bianca.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Bianca.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Bianca.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Bianca.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Bianca.wav.ogg"}]}}}